# shadow_lower bootstrap — edit source, then promote

## Source of truth

- Edit only `cc/shadow/*.ccs` / `*.cch`.
- Committed `cc/bootstrap/shadow_lower/vN/` is **regenerate-only**. Never hand-edit `vN/include/*.h`, `vN/shadow_lower.c`, or patch `last-good`'s tree in place to "land" a fix.

## Ship loop (required when face changes should stick)

```bash
# 1. Edit cc/shadow/*.cch
# 2. Rebuild lowerer from sources (seed re-lowers .ccs)
make -C cc SHADOW_LOWER_SOURCE=ccs ../out/cc/bin/shadow_lower
# 3. Snapshot (+ host-cc smoke)
./scripts/snapshot_shadow_lower.sh --smoke
# 4. Promote → new vN, flip last-good
./scripts/promote_shadow_bootstrap.sh
# 5. Human-gated commit of last-good + vN
```

Default `make -C cc` builds from `last-good` (`SHADOW_LOWER_SOURCE=bootstrap`). That does **not** pick up uncommitted `.cch` edits until you ccs-rebuild and promote.

## Faces vs bootstrap

- `out/include/cc/shadow/*.h` is a **build product** (seeded from `last-good`, copied into `latest/` by snapshot). Do not `cp` raw `*.cch` onto those paths (include spelling / rewrite mismatch).
- Standalone re-lower of some faces hangs — interim iteration via an `out/include` face patch matching the `.cch` is allowed **only as a local build aid**. It is not a substitute for snapshot/promote. Never copy that patch into an existing `vN/`.

